.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine-page-rename 1  "rename " 
.SH NAME
tine\-page\-rename \- Rename a page and rewrite references, as the app does. An existing destination refuses; merges require confirmation in the app
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine page rename\fR [\fB\-g\fR|\fB\-\-graph\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-rev\fR] [\fB\-\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIOLD\fR> <\fINEW\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rename a page and rewrite references, as the app does. An existing destination refuses; merges require confirmation in the app
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-graph\fR \fI<GRAPH>\fR
The graph. Defaults to $TINE_GRAPH, else the graph folder around the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the typed result (schema tine.cli/1) as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-rev\fR \fI<REV>\fR
Unsupported for graph\-wide rename; supplying this option refuses without changes
.TP
\fB\-\-run\fR \fI<RUN>\fR
Unsupported for graph\-wide rename; supplying this option (or a nonempty TINE_RUN) refuses without changes. End/unset the run before renaming
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTINE_RUN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIOLD\fR>

.TP
<\fINEW\fR>

